<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Powershell on cesun.life</title><link>https://example.org/tags/powershell/</link><description>Recent content in Powershell on cesun.life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 04 Dec 2021 17:34:29 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://example.org/tags/powershell/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>PowerShell Splatting and Hashtable Values</title><link>https://example.org/powershell-splatting/</link><pubDate>Sat, 04 Dec 2021 17:34:29 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://example.org/powershell-splatting/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;PowerShell splatting passes a hashtable or array as named or positional arguments.
It avoids repeating long parameter lists and keeps configuration separate from a
command invocation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="splatting-powershell-commands"&gt;
 Splatting PowerShell Commands
 &lt;a href="#splatting-powershell-commands" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prefix a hashtable variable with &lt;code&gt;@&lt;/code&gt; at the call site:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;powershell&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$request = @{
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; Uri = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;https://api.example.test/items&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; Method = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;Get&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; Headers = @{ Accept = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;application/json&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; TimeoutSec = &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Invoke-RestMethod @request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hashtable keys must match parameter names, including supported aliases. Splatting
does not expand arbitrary strings into shell syntax; PowerShell binds the resulting
values as typed command arguments.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>